X86 x86-announce-sb-main
(* Reduced from jit/reduced/x86-main.reduced.asm.
   Protocol is the one pinned down by tla/epoch/fixes/CasAnnounceOneReader.tla.

   P0 reader    : claim the slot (locked RMW on tid), PLAIN-store the announce
                  into lce, re-announce in ProtectAndDrain, then test whether
                  the object is still linked before dereferencing it.
   P1 reclaimer : unlink the object, bump CurrentEpoch (locked RMW -- this
                  drains P1's store buffer), then scan the epoch table.

   Store buffering: P1 is already fenced between its unlink store and its scan
   load, because the epoch bump sits between them. P0 is NOT: its announce is a
   plain store and nothing separates it from the load of `unlinked`. So the
   announce may still be buffered when P1 scans.

   Violated when P1 misses the announce (reads lce=0, so it computes a
   SafeToReclaimEpoch that covers the trigger and frees) while P0 sees the
   object as still linked and dereferences it. *)
{ lce=0; tid=0; cur=1; unlinked=0; }
 P0                | P1                ;
 MOV EDX,$1        | MOV [unlinked],$1 ;
 XCHG [tid],EDX    | MOV EDX,$2        ;
 MOV [lce],$1      | XCHG [cur],EDX    ;
 MOV [lce],$2      | MOV EBX,[lce]     ;
 MOV ECX,[unlinked]|                   ;
exists (0:ECX=0 /\ 1:EBX=0)